        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "To see that $n$ divides $a_n$, factor $n$ as $2^k m$, with $m$ odd. Then note that $k \\leq n \\leq n(n-1)/2$, and that there exists $i \\leq m-1$ such that $m$ divides $2^i-1$, namely $i = \\phi(m)$ (Euler's totient function: the number of integers in $\\{1, \\ldots, m\\}$ relatively prime to $m$).",
          "block_bbox": [
            314,
            220,
            1253,
            467
          ],
          "block_id": 1,
