        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "B−1 The answer is 1/3. Let G be the point obtained by reflecting C about the line AB. Since  $ \\angle ADC = \\frac{\\pi - \\theta}{2} $, we find that  $ \\angle BDE = \\pi - \\theta - \\angle ADC = \\frac{\\pi - \\theta}{2} = \\angle ADC = \\pi - \\angle BDC = \\pi - \\angle BDG $, so that E, D, G are collinear. Hence",
          "block_bbox": [
            230,
            497,
            1251,
            740
          ],
          "block_id": 2,
          "block_order": 2,
          "group_id": 2,
          "block_polygon_points": [
            [
              230.0,
              497.0
            ],
            [
              1251.0,
              497.0
            ],
            [
              1251.0,
              740.0
            ],
            [
              230.0,
              740.0
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "block_label": "display_formula",
          "block_content": " $$ \\left|E F\\right|=\\frac{\\left|B E\\right|}{\\left|B C\\right|}=\\frac{\\left|B E\\right|}{\\left|B G\\right|}=\\frac{\\sin(\\theta/2)}{\\sin(3\\theta/2)}, $$ ",
          "block_bbox": [
            424,
            773,
            1041,
            885
          ],
          "block_id": 3,
          "block_order": 3,
          "group_id": 3,
